ENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"U4X-tzwvTzW8uWxs2KIPtg","review_id":"heB6Ck3auVKV57yzo8Ef-A","date":"2015-06-21T23:06:28","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9385506510734558,"text_excerpt":"First time to eat here. This place is at the corner of Chartres and St. Louis. Not fancy by any means but it has a good feel about the place. The wait was not long, we were seated in a few minutes although almost every table was already full of diners. One of us had the Crab Cake Maspero and I had Blackened Jambalaya with Chicken. The Crab Cakes are served on a bed of sautéed spinach, heirloom tomato, mushrooms and onions, topped with a housemade sauce. This particular food meal was rated the best we had in New Orleans this time. The Blackened Jambalaya was also very good. It has sausage and chicken with good cajun seasoning to bring out the best of the food. I would say that we have miss..."},{"business_id":"U4X-tzwvTzW8uWxs2KIPtg","review_id":"8-GhG0sqzHDlBXGCJBhFfA","date":"2017-06-15T18:29:56","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9381399154663086,"text_excerpt":"Located right in the middle of the French Quarter, I thought that this place was great! We ordered the crab claws as an appetizer, which were delicious. They were more citrus-y than I'm used to, but it was a welcomed flavor and the dish overall was well seasoned. I ordered the oyster pasta and the cream sauce was soooo goood. The restaurant was pretty busy, but our waitress and the other waiters were very attentive and made sure our drinks were refilled and we were satisfied with our food. My friend ordered the shrimp tortellini, which was good, but the shrimp weren't deveined, so she wasn't very happy about that. I guess that's really more of a preference thing, but note that if it is yo..."},{"business_id":"U4X-tzwvTzW8uWxs2KIPtg","review_id":"6-_xuk1hlMrlcsMUozrSoQ","date":"2011-11-03T01:12:07","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9368574023246765,"text_excerpt":"Woot. Decently priced Cajun and Creole food in the heart of the Quarter with no wait on a Saturday night? Awesometown! Our server was a sweetheart. She was friendly, informed and prompt. The red beans and rice were bomb! My bf had chicken parmesan and it was southern fried chicken parmesan with angel hair pasta and so tasty! Will definitely return here. If you can get a window seat, ask for one so you can watch all the people walking by. =)"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"U4X-tzwvTzW8uWxs2KIPtg","photo_id":"uALWt7wuXzXUiJuh40nuNQ","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/uALWt7wuXzXUiJuh40nuNQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8729168176651001},{"business_id":"U4X-tzwvTzW8uWxs2KIPtg","photo_id":"TdPTHnPcV-AiZ0O1JUc-eA","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/TdPTHnPcV-AiZ0O1JUc-eA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8729026913642883},{"business_id":"U4X-tzwvTzW8uWxs2KIPtg","photo_id":"7leT18K_DGS9WdyN7Qw_VQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/7leT18K_DGS9WdyN7Qw_VQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8419294357299805},{"business_id":"U4X-tzwvTzW8u